From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:52:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: defconfig: Build in the Allwinner sun50i cpufreq
 driver

The sun50i cpufreq driver matches the root compatible and has no device
of its own, so as a module it is never loaded automatically. Without it
there are no CPU frequency policies, and the CPU cooling devices and the
A733 DSU devfreq driver, which wait for them, never come up. Build it
in, as commit 5243fc3f7395 ("arm64: defconfig: Enable cpufreq for
MediaTek") did for the MediaTek driver.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards without udev; the CPU
frequency policies and the CPU cooling devices come up on their own, both
clusters run at the pinned rate, and the DSU devfreq driver binds at once.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index 4ea04aba246f..ab1586d3fc98 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_USERSPACE=y
 CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_ONDEMAND=y
 CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_CONSERVATIVE=m
 CONFIG_CPUFREQ_DT=y
-CONFIG_ARM_ALLWINNER_SUN50I_CPUFREQ_NVMEM=m
+CONFIG_ARM_ALLWINNER_SUN50I_CPUFREQ_NVMEM=y
 CONFIG_ARM_APPLE_SOC_CPUFREQ=m
 CONFIG_ARM_ARMADA_37XX_CPUFREQ=y
 CONFIG_ARM_SCPI_CPUFREQ=y
